# Cosmetic guard after the pre-tag identity rewrite.
#
# The rewrite (git filter-repo --mailmap) already collapsed the two historical
# author identities into one, so this file changes nothing about the current
# history. It exists so that if a commit ever lands from a stale local git config
# again — which happened once during the rewrite itself, when the remap commit was
# authored with the old work email and had to be amended — git's own tooling
# displays it correctly instead of quietly showing a third contributor.
#
# It is a display guard, not a fix. The real guards are the local git config and
# GitHub's "block command line pushes that expose my email".
